<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Recruiter Incentive Simulator</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=DM+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700;800&family=DM+Mono:wght@400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
:root {
  --bg: #0a0e1a; --surface: #111525; --surface2: #141830;
  --border: #1e2438; --border-active: #4338ca;
  --text: #e8eaed; --text2: #9ca3af; --text3: #6b7280;
  --accent: #818cf8; --accent-deep: #3730a3;
  --green: #10b981; --green-bg: rgba(16,185,129,0.08); --green-border: rgba(16,185,129,0.2);
  --red: #ef4444; --red-bg: rgba(239,68,68,0.08); --red-border: rgba(239,68,68,0.2);
  --amber: #f59e0b; --indigo: #6366f1; --lavender: #a5b4fc;
}
* { margin:0; padding:0; box-sizing:border-box; }
body { font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif; background:var(--bg); color:var(--text); min-height:100vh; }
.container { max-width:1140px; margin:0 auto; padding:20px 16px; }
.header h1 { font-size:22px; font-weight:800; letter-spacing:-0.03em; }
.header p { font-size:13px; color:var(--text3); margin-top:4px; }
.layout { display:grid; grid-template-columns:310px 1fr; gap:20px; margin-top:20px; }

.left-panel { background:var(--surface); border-radius:14px; padding:20px; border:1px solid var(--border); align-self:start; position:sticky; top:20px; }
.panel-title { font-size:12px; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.08em; margin-bottom:14px; }

.how-it-works { background:var(--bg); border-radius:10px; padding:14px; border:1px solid var(--border); margin-bottom:20px; font-size:11px; color:var(--text2); line-height:1.65; }
.how-it-works strong { color:var(--text); font-weight:600; }
.how-it-works .hw-item { margin-bottom:8px; }
.how-it-works .hw-item:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }

.section-label { font-size:11px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text3); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.08em; margin-bottom:10px; margin-top:4px; }

.slider-group { margin-bottom:18px; }
.slider-header { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:baseline; margin-bottom:5px; }
.slider-label { font-size:12.5px; font-weight:600; color:#c8ccd4; }
.slider-value { font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text); font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; }
.slider-pct { font-size:11px; color:var(--text3); font-weight:400; }
.slider-input { width:100%; accent-color:var(--indigo); height:6px; cursor:pointer; -webkit-appearance:none; background:#1e2438; border-radius:3px; outline:none; }
.slider-input::-webkit-slider-thumb { -webkit-appearance:none; width:16px; height:16px; border-radius:50%; background:var(--indigo); cursor:pointer; }
.slider-range { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; font-size:10px; color:var(--text3); margin-top:2px; }

.toggle-group { margin-bottom:18px; }
.toggle-label { font-size:12.5px; font-weight:600; color:#c8ccd4; margin-bottom:8px; }
.toggle-row { display:flex; gap:0; border-radius:8px; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid #2d3348; }
.toggle-btn { flex:1; padding:8px 4px; font-size:11.5px; font-weight:400; font-family:'DM Sans',sans-serif; background:var(--surface2); color:var(--text3); border:none; cursor:pointer; transition:all 0.15s; }
.toggle-btn.active { background:var(--accent-deep); color:#e0e7ff; font-weight:700; }

.assumptions-box { background:var(--bg); border-radius:8px; padding:10px 12px; border:1px solid var(--border); margin-top:4px; }
.assumptions-box .ab-title { font-size:10px; color:var(--text3); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; margin-bottom:6px; font-weight:600; }
.assumptions-box .ab-row { font-size:11px; color:var(--text2); line-height:1.7; }
.assumptions-box .ab-val { color:var(--text); font-weight:600; font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; }

/* Right panel */
.current-banner { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:16px; margin-bottom:16px; display:grid; grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr); gap:12px; }
.cb-label { font-size:10px; color:var(--text3); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; }
.cb-value { font-size:20px; font-weight:800; margin-top:2px; }
.cb-sub { font-size:11px; color:#787f8c; margin-top:2px; }

.result-card { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border-active); border-radius:14px; padding:20px; position:relative; overflow:hidden; margin-bottom:16px; }
.result-card::before { content:''; position:absolute; top:0; left:0; right:0; height:2px; background:linear-gradient(90deg,#6366f1,#818cf8); }
.result-title { font-size:15px; font-weight:700; color:#e0e7ff; margin-bottom:4px; }
.result-sub { font-size:12px; color:var(--text3); margin-bottom:16px; font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; }

.delta-box { border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px; margin-bottom:16px; }
.delta-box.pos { background:var(--green-bg); border:1px solid var(--green-border); }
.delta-box.neg { background:var(--red-bg); border:1px solid var(--red-border); }
.delta-label { font-size:10px; color:var(--text3); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; margin-bottom:2px; }
.delta-value { font-size:28px; font-weight:800; }
.delta-value.pos { color:var(--green); }
.delta-value.neg { color:var(--red); }
.delta-aside { font-size:11px; color:var(--text2); margin-top:4px; }

.section-box { background:var(--bg); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:10px; padding:14px 16px; margin-bottom:14px; }
.section-box-title { font-size:12px; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; margin-bottom:10px; }
.section-box-note { font-size:11px; color:var(--text3); margin-bottom:10px; font-style:italic; }

.decomp-row { display:flex; justify-content:space-between; align-items:center; padding:4px 0; font-size:12.5px; }
.decomp-row .dl { color:var(--text2); }
.decomp-row .dv { font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; font-weight:600; }
.decomp-row .dv.pos { color:var(--green); }
.decomp-row .dv.neg { color:var(--red); }
.decomp-row .dv.neutral { color:var(--text2); }
.decomp-row .dv.zero { color:var(--text3); }
.decomp-divider { border-top:1px solid var(--border); margin:8px 0; }
.decomp-row.total .dl { color:var(--text); font-weight:600; }
.decomp-row.total .dv { font-size:14px; }

.punchline { background:var(--green-bg); border:1px solid var(--green-border); border-radius:8px; padding:10px 14px; margin-top:10px; font-size:12px; color:var(--text2); line-height:1.6; }
.punchline.warning { background:var(--red-bg); border-color:var(--red-border); }
.punchline strong { color:var(--text); }
.punchline .val-green { color:var(--green); font-weight:700; font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; }
.punchline .val-red { color:var(--red); font-weight:700; font-family:'DM Mono',monospace; }

.totals-grid { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr; gap:12px; padding-top:14px; border-top:1px solid var(--border); }
.total-item .ti-label { font-size:9px; color:var(--text3); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; }
.total-item .ti-value { font-size:16px; font-weight:700; color:var(--text); margin-top:2px; }

.methodology { background:var(--surface); border:1px solid var(--border); border-radius:12px; padding:16px; }
.methodology h3 { font-size:13px; font-weight:700; color:var(--accent); text-transform:uppercase; letter-spacing:0.06em; margin-bottom:12px; }
.methodology p { font-size:12px; color:var(--text2); line-height:1.7; margin-bottom:8px; }
.methodology p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }
.methodology strong { color:#c8ccd4; }

@media (max-width:800px) {
  .layout { grid-template-columns:1fr; }
  .left-panel { position:static; }
  .current-banner { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }
  .totals-grid { grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; }
}
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="container">
  <div class="header">
    <h1>Recruiter Incentive Simulator</h1>
    <p>168 recruiters · 7 Team Leads · 15 Managers · 4,152 placements · March 2026 actuals</p>
  </div>

  <div class="layout">
    <!-- LEFT PANEL -->
    <div class="left-panel">
      <div class="panel-title">Controls</div>

      <div class="how-it-works">
        <div class="hw-item"><strong>Base per-placement incentive</strong> is held fixed at the current FY26 slab rates. At all-zero settings below, the proposed scheme costs exactly the same as the current one.</div>
        <div class="hw-item"><strong>Retention bonus</strong> is the new component: a per-month payment for each month a placed worker continues in the role, paid on top of the per-placement base. Revenue comes from the extra month of tenure; cost accrues across all months including the ones where the worker would have stayed anyway.</div>
        <div class="hw-item"><strong>Sourcing bonus</strong> is paid once per cross-recruiter placement — when a recruiter shares a candidate who gets placed by a different recruiter. Set as a fraction of the placer's per-placement base rate.</div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-label">Retention Bonus (per month per placement)</div>

      <div class="slider-group">
        <div class="slider-header">
          <span class="slider-label">Slab 1 placements</span>
          <span class="slider-value" id="y1-val">₹20 <span class="slider-pct">(14% of base)</span></span>
        </div>
        <input class="slider-input" type="range" id="y1" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="20">
        <div class="slider-range"><span>₹0</span><span>₹100</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="slider-group">
        <div class="slider-header">
          <span class="slider-label">Slab 2 placements</span>
          <span class="slider-value" id="y2-val">₹20 <span class="slider-pct">(11% of base)</span></span>
        </div>
        <input class="slider-input" type="range" id="y2" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="20">
        <div class="slider-range"><span>₹0</span><span>₹100</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="slider-group">
        <div class="slider-header">
          <span class="slider-label">Slab 3 placements</span>
          <span class="slider-value" id="y3-val">₹20 <span class="slider-pct">(7% of base)</span></span>
        </div>
        <input class="slider-input" type="range" id="y3" min="0" max="100" step="5" value="20">
        <div class="slider-range"><span>₹0</span><span>₹100</span></div>
      </div>

      <div class="section-label" style="margin-top:8px;">Sourcing Bonus</div>

      <div class="toggle-group">
        <div class="toggle-label">Amount as a fraction of placer's base rate</div>
        <div class="toggle-row">
          <button class="toggle-btn" data-group="zfac" data-val="1">Full base</button>
          <button class="toggle-btn" data-group="zfac" data-val="0.667">2/3 of base</button>
          <button class="toggle-btn active" data-group="zfac" data-val="0.5">Half of base</button>
          <button class="toggle-btn" data-group="zfac" data-val="0.333">1/3 of base</button>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="assumptions-box">
        <div class="ab-title">Assumed Behavioural Response</div>
        <div class="ab-row">Retention improvement from bonus: <span class="ab-val">+1 month</span></div>
        <div class="ab-row">Placements sourced cross-recruiter: <span class="ab-val">5% of all</span></div>
        <div class="ab-row">Of those, share that are net new: <span class="ab-val">50%</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- RIGHT PANEL -->
    <div class="right-panel">
      <div id="result-area"></div>

      <div class="methodology">
        <h3>How the Numbers Are Calculated</h3>

        <p><strong>Per-placement base incentive (unchanged from current scheme):</strong> Each recruiter's base pay uses marginal slab brackets — the first set of placements at the Slab 1 rate, the next set at the Slab 2 rate, and so on. Placements with a hiring/sourcing fee (HSR) and without it are counted on separate ladders. Enterprise Consumer/BFSI slabs break at 35 and 70 placements; Airtel at 30 and 60; Corporate at 25 and 50. HSR rates are ₹150/200/300; non-HSR rates are ₹130/175/250. Recruiters below their vertical's target earn nothing. Because the base incentive is identical to the current scheme, it cancels out — every rupee of cost change comes from the retention and sourcing bonuses.</p>

        <p><strong>Retention bonus (new cost, accrues monthly):</strong> For each eligible recruiter, every placement earns an additional amount per month the worker stays (capped at 12 months). The per-month rate depends on which slab tier that placement falls in. Team Leads and Managers receive the same per-month rates, applied to their attributed placements (capped at 100). The assumed improvement is that workers stay 1 additional month on average, generating extra markup revenue for the firm but also incurring retention bonus cost across all months of the worker's tenure — including the months they would have stayed without the bonus.</p>

        <p><strong>Sourcing bonus (new cost, paid once at placement):</strong> 5% of all placements (not just target-eligible) are assumed to be cross-recruiter sourced, since a recruiter can share a candidate regardless of whether they meet their own placement target. Each cross-sourced placement carries a one-time sourcing bonus set as a fraction of the placer's average base rate. Of these, half are assumed to be genuinely new placements (creating new revenue and new placement costs), and half are substitution (same total placements, just the sourcing bonus cost).</p>

        <p><strong>Revenue:</strong> For each recruiter, monthly revenue = average monthly markup per placement × number of placements. The assumed 1 additional month of retention increases the number of months each worker stays, adding one extra month of markup revenue per placement. Net new placements from cross-sourcing also generate markup revenue and sourcing fees.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

